    "description": "## Source of truth\n\nhttps://jumpr.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/JK/pages/269090817/03+User+Stories+Jira+Disposition\n\n## Outcome\n\nActive Deals with no qualifying activity for the configured number of calendar days become Inactive through a simple scheduled sweep.\n\n## Eligibility\n\n* First Activated Date + Last Sign-Up First Click Date determine the activity baseline.\n* Default threshold = 90 days, configurable.\n* Exactly N days old remains Active; older than N days qualifies.\n* Only current Status = Active can qualify.\n\n## Inactive behavior\n\n* Scheduled Flow sets Status = Inactive.\n* WAGR-486 stamps lifecycle tracking.\n* WAGR-455 queues the status sync.\n* **Inactive is informational only.**\n* Do not deactivate Affiliate Links.\n* Do not alter DRAs.\n* CMS may store/display Inactive but must not treat it like Pause.\n* Qualifying new activity may return the Deal to Active through WAGR-498.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Draft/Paused/Closed/Archived/Inactive Deals never qualify.\n2. 90-day boundary behavior remains as designed.\n3. Inactivation sends the new status but leaves Affiliate Links and DRAs unchanged.\n4. The scheduled flow performs no per-Deal Sign-Up query.\n\n",
